/-!
# The Čech complex of a restriction cover is the Zariski Čech complex on the ambient scheme

Fix a global crystalline situation `(p, (S, I, γ), X)` and an object `A = (U, T, δ)` of the small
crystalline site `Cris(X/S)`.  The covering families of `Cris(X/S)` are generated by the families
of restrictions `A|_{V_i} ⟶ A` attached to an open cover `{V_i}` of the ambient scheme `T`
(`Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.restrictCoverage`), and the iterated fibre products of
such a family are again restrictions,

`A|_{V_{i₀}} ×_A ⋯ ×_A A|_{V_{i_p}} = A|_{V_{i₀} ∩ ⋯ ∩ V_{i_p}}`,

by `SmallSite.CrystallineThickening.isLimit_restrictOpenFan`.  A presheaf `I` on `Cris(X/S)`
therefore takes, on the degree-`p` terms of the Čech complex of that family, exactly the values
its restriction `(restrictOpenFunctor A).op ⋙ I` takes on the degree-`p` terms of the Zariski
Čech complex of `{V_i}` on `T`.  This file proves that those identifications are compatible with
the differentials, so the two Čech complexes are isomorphic, and uses the isomorphism to compute
the Čech cohomology of the abelian sheaf underlying a locally quasi-coherent `𝒪_{X/S}`-module on
a standard restriction cover of an object with affine ambient scheme: it vanishes in positive
degrees.  That vanishing is the Čech-vanishing input `hCech` of [Stacks, Tag 03F9], which is how
[Stacks, Tag 07JJ] is proved.

## Main definitions

Everything crystalline lives in `Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.SmallSite`, mostly in
its `CrystallineThickening` namespace.

* `CrystallineThickening.restrictOpenOverFunctor` — the restrictions of `A` to the opens of its
  ambient scheme, read as a functor into the slice `Over A`.
* `CrystallineThickening.restrictOpenHypercover` — the family of those restrictions as a
  `CategoryTheory.PreZeroHypercover`, at an arbitrary index universe.
* `CrystallineThickening.restrictOpenPiFan`, `isLimit_restrictOpenPiFan`,
  `restrictOpenPiIso` — the degreewise identification of an iterated fibre product of
  restrictions with the restriction to a categorical product of opens.
* `CrystallineThickening.cechSimplicialObjectRestrictIso` — the identification of the two Čech
  simplicial formal coproducts.
* `CrystallineThickening.cechComplexRestrictIso` and `cechCohomologyRestrictIso` — **the
  identification of the two Čech complexes, and of their cohomology.**
* `Stacks.CechSite.formalCoproductMap` and `Stacks.CechSite.evalOpFormalCoproductMapIso` — the
  functoriality of `CategoryTheory.Limits.FormalCoproduct` in the ambient category, and its
  compatibility with evaluating a presheaf; `Stacks.CechSite.natIsoRightOp` is the action of
  `CategoryTheory.Functor.rightOp` on a natural isomorphism.

## Main results

* `pi_opens_eq_iInf` — a categorical product of opens of a scheme is their infimum.
* `CrystallineThickening.subsingleton_overHom_restrictOpen` — **at most one morphism of `Over A`
  lands in a given restriction of `A`.**  This is what makes every naturality square below free.
* `CrystallineThickening.isSubterminal_overMk_restrictOpenHom` — the same fact as
  **subterminality of a restriction in `Over A`**, which is the hypothesis under which the
  alternating Čech cochains of a covering family of a site form a subcomplex
  (`StacksFrontier/CategoryTheory/Sites/CechComplexAlternating.lean`).
* `CrystallineThickening.toSheaf_moduleRestriction_obj` and `abelianSheaf_obj` — the sections
  lemmas: the abelian presheaf underlying the restriction `F_T` of a sheaf of `𝒪_{X/S}`-modules
  to the ambient scheme of `A` is `(restrictOpenFunctor A).op ⋙ F.val.presheaf`, and the abelian
  sheaf `SmallSite.abelianSheaf F` of the coefficient universe `u + 1` is
  `F.val.presheaf ⋙ AddCommGrpCat.uliftFunctor`.  Both hold by `rfl`.
* `CrystallineThickening.isZero_cechCohomology_restrictOpenHypercover` — transport of Čech
  vanishing from the ambient scheme to `Cris(X/S)`.
* `isZero_cechCohomology_abelianSheaf_of_isStandardOpenCover` and its `_ulift` variant —
  **positive-degree Čech vanishing for a locally quasi-coherent module on a standard restriction
  cover of an object with affine ambient scheme.**

## Implementation notes

**Why the naturality is free.**  The structure morphism `A|_V ⟶ A` of a restriction is a
monomorphism (`SmallSite.CrystallineThickening.mono_restrictOpenHom`), so a morphism of `Over A`
with target `Over.mk (A.restrictOpenHom V)` is determined by its source: the full subcategory of
`Over A` spanned by the restrictions of `A` is *thin*.  Every naturality square appearing in the
comparison has a restriction as its target — in the Čech simplicial object the degree-`p` term is
the restriction to an intersection, by `isLimit_restrictOpenFan` — so
`subsingleton_overHom_restrictOpen` discharges all of them, and no computation with the
alternating-sum differential is needed anywhere.  For the same reason `restrictOpenOverFunctor`
needs no proof of its functor laws.

**Why both Čech constructions are the same shape.**  `Stacks.CechSite.cechComplex` of a
`PreZeroHypercover` and Mathlib's `CategoryTheory.cechComplexFunctor` of a family of objects of
a category with finite products are both
`CategoryTheory.Limits.FormalCoproduct.cochainComplexFunctor` applied to a simplicial formal
coproduct whose degree-`p` index type is the type of `(p+1)`-tuples of indices, and whose
structure maps act on that index type by composition with the simplicial operator.  The two
simplicial formal coproducts live in `FormalCoproduct (Over A)` and `FormalCoproduct T.Opens`
respectively; `formalCoproductMap (restrictOpenOverFunctor A)` carries the second to the first
category, and `cechSimplicialObjectRestrictIso` is an isomorphism there.  Transporting it to the
level of complexes costs nothing beyond `evalOpFormalCoproductMapIso`, which is `Iso.refl`: the
two evaluations are definitionally the same functor.

**Where `⨅` meets `∏ᶜ`.**  `isLimit_restrictOpenFan` names the product
`A.restrictOpen (⨅ a, V a)`, while `CategoryTheory.cechComplexFunctor` names it with the
categorical product `∏ᶜ` of the opens.  `pi_opens_eq_iInf` identifies the two — an isomorphism of
opens is an equality, the opens of a space being partially ordered — and
`isLimit_restrictOpenPiFan` transports the limit along it.  The transport needs no coherence
proof, again by `subsingleton_overHom_restrictOpen`.

**Kernel cost.**  `cechSimplicialObjectRestrictIso` is built as `asIso` of an explicit morphism
of simplicial objects rather than by `CategoryTheory.NatIso.ofComponents`, and the index-level
half of each naturality square is proved pointwise through
`CategoryTheory.Limits.FormalCoproduct.hom_ext_iff'`.  Both choices are forced: the
whole-function form of that equation, `((cechSimplicialObject _).map g ≫ _).f = _`, is true by
`rfl` but the *kernel* does not finish checking it, while the pointwise form is immediate.

**Index universes.**  The covering families of `restrictCoverage` are indexed by `Type (u + 1)`,
so the Čech-vanishing hypothesis of [Stacks, Tag 03F9] at the coefficient universe `u + 1` is
about `PreZeroHypercover.{u + 1}`.  The Zariski side, on the other hand, has coefficients in
`AddCommGrpCat.{u}`, which has no `Type (u + 1)`-indexed products.  `restrictOpenHypercover` is
therefore stated at a free index universe, the comparison with it, and the coefficient lift to
`AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1}` is performed on the *crystalline* side at index universe `0`, through
`Stacks.CechSite.isZero_cechCohomology_comp_coefficients`; the index type is then lifted by
`Stacks.CategoryTheory.CechComplex.isZero_homology_of_ulift`.

**What is not proved.**  The Čech vanishing is proved for a *standard* restriction cover — the
restrictions to the basic opens `T_{g i}` of a finite family of sections `g` of an affine `T`
whose basic opens cover `Spec Γ(T, 𝒪_T)` — and not for an arbitrary cover of `A` by restrictions
to affine opens.  The engine used is [Stacks, Tag 01X9],
`Stacks.Cohomology.Cech.isZero_cechCohomology_of_isStandardOpenCover`, which is stated for
standard covers and in the `CategoryTheory.cechComplexFunctor` spelling.  Getting the arbitrary
affine cover would need [Stacks, Tag 01XD] instead, and two things it does not come with:
`Stacks.Cohomology.CechAffineCover.isIso_cechCohomologyToCohomology_app_of_isAffineOpen` is
stated for the module-valued Čech cohomology of `Stacks.Cohomology.CechDerived`, not for
`CategoryTheory.cechComplexFunctor`, and its index type is `Type u` while a member of
`restrictCoverage` is indexed by `Type (u + 1)` — a `Type (u + 1)`-indexed family of opens of `T`
factors through its range, but the Čech complexes of a family and of its range are compared only
by a refinement map, whose effect on cohomology is [Stacks, Tag 03F7] and is not available here.
So nothing in this file carries the tag `07JJ`.

## References

